WEBVTT

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:10.200
That was Elizabeth. Do you want us to her, Tim?

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:26.260
Are you all right, Elizabeth?

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:28.360
Yes, thanks. She got here just in time.

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:29.980
Bullying yobs. I wish...

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.800
weren't so peaceful, then I'd show them.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:34.280
It wasn't their fault, Stephen. I don't think they knew what they were doing.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:36.440
They were quite quiet until the picture changed.

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:38.380
Yeah, we were watching it. We saw a change.

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:40.740
The one in the classroom. That one.

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:57.460
Of course, the best thing to do in those circumstances

00:02:57.460 --> 00:02:58.560
is just to jaunt away.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:02:59.980
I know I should have done.

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:02.680
It's all so new to me, the time I didn't think of it.

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:09.820
Oh, no, Stephen, what have you done to the video call?

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.020
If I found it like this, someone must have smashed it.

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:13.720
And the recording tape is missing.

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:15.520
It wouldn't have been the school caretaker.

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:16.800
He'd just have locked us that way.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:18.080
I called the police.

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:19.270
What about Robert?

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:21.040
No, not necessarily.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.320
That painting seems to control people.

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:27.350
Perhaps it, or someone else, is controlling Robert.

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:29.980
Either way, I think we ought to keep an eye on Robert for now.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:35.850
now on he's our only lead the paintings are spreading so is the wearing of blue and green

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:41.530
badges and so is the violence something's taking over people's minds and robbing them of their

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:47.220
reason and i'm afraid it is happening all over the world in some countries it is far in advance of

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:53.350
the stage we have reached look at this film of battles between blue and green supporters in tokyo

00:03:53.690 --> 00:03:58.920
some reports say that the police themselves took sides some with the blue and some with the green

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:07.500
Okay, so it's a real and dangerous menace that's rather crept up on us in all the excitement of Elizabeth joining us.

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:09.060
That makes me feel as if it's my fault, in a way.

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:09.980
No, of course not.

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:13.360
Look, what I want you to do tomorrow is keep an eye on Robert.

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:15.550
I'm going to go back to that shop where we bought the painting.

00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:20.850
Give us a pound for the watch, mate.

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:22.350
Take your watch away, boy.

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:24.650
I don't want eight and a half carat gold.

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:25.350
Go on.

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:26.350
75 pounds in.

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:27.210
Waiting my time.

00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:27.570
Go on.

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:28.450
Oh, you're an old miser.

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:29.440
Thank you very much.

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:29.760
Go on.

00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:38.170
Yes, I tell you, no, I'm not buying anything.

00:04:38.350 --> 00:04:39.410
I'm not selling anything either.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:41.920
I was interested in the painting you have.

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:44.370
I was interested in the painting you have in the window.

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:45.670
Ah, the painting in the window.

00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:52.550
Is this the one, Sonny?

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:54.110
Oh, no, no, it's not that one.

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:55.730
Well, make up your mind, boy. Which one do you want?

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:57.090
It's a bit difficult to describe, really.

00:04:57.250 --> 00:04:59.550
It's got a white wood frame and, um...

00:04:59.570 --> 00:04:59.650
White?

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:01.040
White wood frame.

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:03.360
The weather picture.

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:06.840
You don't want to bother with that boy. It's completely worthless.

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:08.740
He's painted by my grandson.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:09.720
Your grandson?

00:05:10.150 --> 00:05:12.710
Not really my grandson.

00:05:13.150 --> 00:05:14.530
He was adopted.

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:16.650
May I see it?

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:19.870
You don't want to worry about it. It's completely worthless.

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:23.530
Anything's worth money if the customer's prepared to pay for it.

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:33.420
Yes, sir. Well, I think I can get it out for you.

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:36.600
Very good, this big deal.

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:41.050
Clean it up. Yes, that's the one. I'll give you two pounds.

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:44.900
I don't know about that. It's my grandson's own fair work, you know.

00:05:45.260 --> 00:05:47.740
I couldn't let it go for as little as two pounds.

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:49.780
All right, all right. How much? Four pounds.

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:51.060
Two pounds fifty, not a penny more.

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:55.520
Three pounds fifty. I mean, nights of work it took him.

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:57.360
All right, three pounds. There we go. Done.

00:06:05.020 --> 00:06:07.000
I'd like to see your grandson.

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:09.000
Can't. He's not here. He's away at school.

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:22.380
Well, Tim, here it is.

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:25.420
I am not sure it was wise to bring it in here.

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:26.520
Well, neither am I.

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:28.720
Is there any other way you can give it a detailed examination?

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:29.840
No.

00:06:30.510 --> 00:06:33.750
John, we found out something very interesting about Robert.

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:36.060
I wonder if it's the same thing I found out.

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:39.350
Probably. Robert lives at the shop where we saw that other picture.

00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:42.300
Yes. I went over there this afternoon. I met his grandfather.

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:46.450
I bought the painting. The old twister made me pay three quid for it.

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:49.620
And I'm going there after school. I've been invited.

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:05.600
Yes? Are we closed? It's me, Grandfather. I've bought a friend from school.

00:07:05.720 --> 00:07:09.660
A friend? This is Stephen, Grandfather. We're in the same class.

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:13.450
Oh, yes. I sold that picture of yours, my boy.

00:07:14.190 --> 00:07:16.110
Sold it? But I wanted to keep it.

00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:18.650
Oh, but I got you a very good price for it, you see.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:22.960
I got, let's see now, 30 shillings for it.

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:25.620
You mean £1.50, Grandfather.

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:28.840
I don't know anything about that new money, boy. I'll get you the cash.

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:35.020
There we are. I think it's all here.

00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:39.830
There you are. £1.10.

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:43.720
20, 30, 40, and 2.5, make 50.

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:47.280
Thanks, Grandfather. We're going down the cellar.

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:47.850
Oh, yeah?

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:51.090
Come on, Stephen.

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:56.410
I'll give you a shilling for a sweetie instead.

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:00.720
That's it.

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:19.080
busy

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:19.980
Yes.

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:23.040
and boxes of blue and green badges.

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:24.460
Do you make these down here too?

00:08:25.110 --> 00:08:26.570
I have a few friends who help.

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:27.470
And your grandfather.

00:08:28.470 --> 00:08:29.450
He never comes down here.

00:08:31.020 --> 00:08:33.000
He's not really my grandfather, you know.

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:33.660
No?

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:36.930
No, he just looks after me.

00:08:37.510 --> 00:08:38.990
He always has done since I...

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:40.220
Since?

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:45.980
Since as long as I can remember.

00:08:47.060 --> 00:08:49.320
Money comes from somewhere every month and he looks after me.

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:51.200
I call him grandfather.

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:53.280
Well, it is better than an orphanage.

00:08:53.860 --> 00:08:54.060
True.

00:08:55.610 --> 00:08:56.730
Do you know who your parents were?

00:08:57.620 --> 00:08:58.140
Sort of.

00:08:59.360 --> 00:08:59.920
You're lucky, really.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:03.180
I bet your grandfather isn't always turning off the telly.

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:04.760
In the middle of a good horror film.

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:05.570
No.

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:06.680
But we don't have TV.

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:08.800
I wouldn't have time to watch it anyway.

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:10.520
You're a strange one and no mistake.

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:11.580
Hey, robot.

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:14.000
Why are you stirring up this blue and green business?

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:17.130
But it seems to be silly to me. Silly and possibly dangerous.

00:09:17.470 --> 00:09:18.630
I'm not stirring it.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:21.340
I only give the people badges because they want them.

00:09:22.230 --> 00:09:23.630
They asked me for them, you see.

00:09:24.310 --> 00:09:25.430
There's no harm in it.

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:29.010
Well, if you think there's no harm in splitting up people into factions of any kind...

00:09:29.270 --> 00:09:29.970
Really just all just

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:34.040
the colour of a badge. Well, look at Northern Ireland. The blue and the green game is nothing

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:34.580
like that.

00:09:35.270 --> 00:09:36.390
Just a bit of fun, that's all.

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:37.840
Anyway, Stephen.

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:41.850
I brought you here because I thought you and I could be friends.

00:09:43.110 --> 00:09:44.710
We might have more in common than you think.

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:46.140
Yes, we love.

00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:47.050
I'm sorry.

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:48.660
That's all right.

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:50.700
I don't blame you for being curious.

00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:53.680
Give me a hand with these boxes, will you?

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:54.290
Okay?

00:09:55.880 --> 00:09:56.420
Hey, what's that?

00:09:56.950 --> 00:09:57.010
Thank you.

00:09:57.130 --> 00:09:58.010
Just to store them.

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:19.250
Oh, good. Put it up over there, will you?

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:21.420
What have you found out today?

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:22.290
Anything?

00:10:22.530 --> 00:10:23.650
No, nothing so far.

00:10:24.570 --> 00:10:26.830
Tim's just about to give the painting a neutron examination.

00:10:28.220 --> 00:10:28.640
Ready, Tim?

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:29.600
Yes.

00:10:30.250 --> 00:10:32.090
Stand back a bit. This may be dangerous.

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:38.820
I'll start with a fairly gentle probe of neutrino rays.

00:11:04.410 --> 00:11:05.050
What's happened?

00:11:06.940 --> 00:11:07.720
Like soot!

00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:10.360
She's

00:11:11.320 --> 00:11:12.380
You destroyed it, Tim.

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:14.460
I didn't destroy it, Steven.

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:15.970
It destroyed itself.

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:17.590
Wow!

00:11:18.260 --> 00:11:23.360
At first, I felt some resistance to the probe rays, as though the picture were trying to deflect them.

00:11:23.930 --> 00:11:25.130
Then I turned up the power.

00:11:25.690 --> 00:11:26.670
You saw what happened.

00:11:28.090 --> 00:11:29.970
You mean it had a built-in self-destructive eye?

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.920
That is what I surmise, yes.

00:11:33.720 --> 00:11:35.640
Somebody doesn't want us probing into what they're doing.

00:11:36.070 --> 00:11:39.710
I'm afraid I wasn't able to find out anything before the picture disintegrated.

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:44.990
but I'm interested to know that it was equipped to detect and deflect probing rays.

00:11:45.510 --> 00:11:48.030
Even probes that the saps have never heard of.

00:11:48.490 --> 00:11:50.970
and destroy itself should the deflectors fail.

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:53.390
Very sophisticated piece of apparatus.

00:11:54.180 --> 00:11:55.900
Now that you know what you're up against, Tim...

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:57.120
Do you want something to try with this one?

00:11:57.610 --> 00:11:58.690
No, I couldn't get through.

00:11:59.050 --> 00:11:59.890
Hang it up again, Steve.

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:01.760
will keep it under close observation.

00:12:02.020 --> 00:12:02.840
I wish you wouldn't.

