It's about the rent. I'm not paying until the pipe is fixed.

00:19:35.860 --> 00:19:37.120
It's nothing to do with the rent.

00:19:37.360 --> 00:19:40.620
I came in here the other day and bought a painting off you painted by your grandson.

00:19:40.920 --> 00:19:43.420
It's no refund. It's company policy. What's wrong with it, anyway?

00:19:43.580 --> 00:19:45.740
There's nothing wrong with it. I don't want any money from you at all.

00:19:45.840 --> 00:19:47.940
In fact, I might be in a position to give you something.

00:19:48.380 --> 00:19:51.380
I knew it. You're an insurance salesman. Get out.

00:19:51.800 --> 00:19:53.880
I'm not an insurance salesman. I'm a journalist.

00:19:53.980 --> 00:19:54.840
A what? A journalist.

00:19:55.180 --> 00:19:55.520
Journalist.

00:19:55.650 --> 00:19:59.790
I write articles, and I thought I might write an article about your grandson and his amazing paintings.

00:20:00.090 --> 00:20:02.330
I might be able to pay for some information.

00:20:02.660 --> 00:20:04.640
Ah, sir, yes, well, hmm.

00:20:06.020 --> 00:20:08.050
If you'd like to step this way, I'll see.

00:20:09.440 --> 00:20:09.780
This?

00:20:10.260 --> 00:20:10.820
Yes, well, I will.

00:20:13.120 --> 00:20:26.300
No, you cannot see Robert.

00:20:26.560 --> 00:20:27.800
Robert is not in.

00:20:28.170 --> 00:20:29.050
Robert is out.

00:20:30.890 --> 00:20:33.030
Oh, well, maybe I could look down the cellar,

00:20:33.070 --> 00:20:34.670
see where the genius turns out his masterpiece.

00:20:35.590 --> 00:20:38.770
Cannot go down into the cellar unless Robert allows it.

00:20:38.930 --> 00:20:39.750
But he wouldn't know.

00:20:39.870 --> 00:20:40.730
Just one quick look.

00:20:41.190 --> 00:20:42.170
You will go now.

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:44.430
But I just want a quick look.

00:20:44.570 --> 00:20:45.050
I mean, he...

00:20:45.050 --> 00:20:46.730
Time for me to shut the shop.

00:20:46.890 --> 00:20:47.950
You must go now.

00:20:48.300 --> 00:20:48.580
Oh.

00:20:50.310 --> 00:20:53.590
I'll tell him you called. Maybe he will get in touch with you.

00:20:54.310 --> 00:20:54.950
Go now.

00:20:56.260 --> 00:20:56.620
Let's go.

00:21:07.260 --> 00:21:08.380
Now leave him to me.

00:21:08.500 --> 00:21:14.960
I must say he's a strange old geezer.

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:18.280
It's almost as if he's under some sort of hypnotic control.

00:21:18.540 --> 00:21:19.200
Like a zombie.

00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:22.020
Doesn't seem to know what he's doing from one minute to the next.

00:21:41.160 --> 00:21:41.860
Look at it, John.

00:21:45.170 --> 00:21:45.810
Off your hand.

00:21:45.970 --> 00:21:46.890
Leave it alone.

00:21:48.490 --> 00:21:49.370
Get away from that picture.

00:21:51.270 --> 00:21:51.910
Watch it, John.

00:21:52.340 --> 00:21:52.900
Stop it.

00:21:53.000 --> 00:21:53.300
Piss it.

00:21:54.890 --> 00:21:56.960
You're all right, kid.

00:22:04.820 --> 00:22:05.820
You're supposed to put out the lamp.
